11.06
Every time the address of a variable is printed, the address keeps changing.
Why?
The primary reason is ASLR (Address Space Layout Randomization).

''ASLR'' is a security technique that randomizes the memory addresses of areas such as the stack, heap, and libraries when a program is executed.

